Title: Boxes and ids
Author: Tsukuri tests

/* A small original story for the core tests: two Sections, four Scenes,
   one cut and two auto-animated Scenes. */

# The same box

= One box, two screens.

INT. FIRST SCREEN - DAY #first#

A box {id=box cell=tl class=box}
The caption {id=cap cell=bc class=muted visible=false}
Old news {id=old cell=mr class=label}
Footer {id=foot cell=bl class=muted}

[[effects
  r1: show   cap at word("corner").end
  f1: focus  box at word("box", 2).start
  s1: sound  pop at word("box", 2).end +100ms
]]

NARRATOR
(slowly)
This box sits in the corner. The caption says what it is.

NARRATOR
Look at the box.

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. SECOND SCREEN - DAY #second#

A box {id=box cell=mc class=accent}
The new caption {id=cap cell=bc class=muted}
New arrival {id=new cell=tr class=title visible=false}
Footer {id=foot cell=bl class=muted}

[[effects
  s1: sound whoosh at transition.start
  s2: sound ding at box.move.50%
  r1: show new at word("enters").end
  f1: focus new at r1.end +3f
]]

NARRATOR
(pause 0.5)
Same id, new place. A new element enters.

# The cut

> CUT

INT. THIRD SCREEN - DAY #third#

/* a note that is not an effects block */

Fresh start {id=fresh cell=mc class=title}

NARRATOR
(quickly)
Nothing is matched across a cut.

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. FOURTH SCREEN - DAY #fourth#

Fresh start {id=fresh cell=tc class=title}

[[effects
  s1: sound ding at fresh.move.end -50ms
  s2: sound pop at 1.5s because "the title settles on a beat in the music"
]]

NARRATOR
The title moves up.
